hint: `line = f"{item:<10}{price:>8.2f}"`
right: `{item:<10}` pads the name with spaces on the right up to 10 characters, and `{price:>8.2f}` rounds the price to 2 decimals and pads it on the left up to 8 characters, so the decimal points line up from row to row. A width is a minimum, so a longer name like "hot chocolate" isn't cut.
wrong: Put both values in one f-string, each with a format after a colon: `f"{item:<10}{price:>8.2f}"`. `<10` means left-align in 10 characters, and `>8.2f` means right-align in 8 characters with 2 decimals.

